      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f38466a3ea8727b74c9de69|full_name}: i think the main reason for that kind of behaviour is the fact that the bones are used entirely in the form of capsules instead of the ends as spheres. both behaviours can be tricky in some cases (spheres can go around colliders) but the capsules really make things seem really stiff and would encourage people to disregard cutting down on bones in favor for a more pleasant look on bone chain movement.\nbut there are also weird behaviours in some cases where entire bone chains simply freeze with only the root actually moving (or in other cases, a single bone)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
